From af422eeb91c06347647887d0435c43dafea5a55c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: netplay <netplay@localhost>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:29:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 12/42] netplay: lobby with rooms and player names, direct
 connection with relay fallback

With server= in netplay.ini, Host opens a room on the netplay-server and the
others see it as a folder in the OSD file browser, _Netplay/Rooms/<name> -
<game>/<game>.nes; loading the game there joins that room (Join with a game
joins the oldest waiting room with the same md5). The game in a room comes
from the server's games or an own copy found by md5 (index of the games
folder, cached in netplay/index-<core>.txt), and keeps the host's file name so
both sides use the same .sav. name= sets the player name shown in the lobby
and the OSD.

Once paired, the MiSTers try to reach each other directly: the server sends
each the other's public and (private-range) local address and a token; a
PUNCHACK with that token makes the path direct. Session packets go through the
server until then, and again if the direct path is silent for 2 s. direct=no
keeps everything on the relay. The server's RAM folder is now _Netplay with
Server games/ (at most 32 MB) and Rooms/. OSD messages are queued so none is
overwritten unseen. Recording paths are resolved on the main thread, and the
lobby's HTTP fetches can be interrupted by a core change.

T3: host + join through a real server, direct, direct=no, Join same game and
with the same .sav on both sides.
